 "about": "Section 3.3 (I10). Stored passwords: pbkdf2-sha256$<iterations>$<salt>$<hash>, PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-256 over the UTF-8 bytes of the password's NFKC form, a 16-byte salt and a 32-byte output, both standard base64 with padding. Length: 15 to 128 code points under High, 12 to 128 under Standard, counted after NFKC; checked first (password-length). Then password-weak when the lower-cased NFKC text equals a blocked-list line (lower-cased), or contains a context word of 4 or more characters (context_words, the relay's host, the email's local part, all lower-cased). Decoys: normalized = the email with ASCII whitespace trimmed and A to Z lower-cased; mac_i = HMAC-SHA-256(key, lp(normalized, one byte i)) for i 0 to 3, all 4 for every login/begin with an email; lengths = the lengths of the console's registered non-discoverable credential ids, one per id, sorted ascending; length_i = 64 when there are none, else lengths[u32 big-endian of mac_i bytes 0 to 3 mod the count]; id_i = the first length_i bytes of SHA-256(mac_i || u32be(0)) || SHA-256(mac_i || u32be(1)) || ...; slot j holds the account's j-th non-discoverable id (registration order) when it has one, else id_j. lp writes each part as its 4-byte big-endian length, then its bytes.",
 "format": "pbkdf2-sha256$<iterations>$<salt_b64>$<hash_b64>",
